{
  "description": "The feature counters (docs/control-port.md#counters): the snapshot carries the graph's counters and each node's; counters.changed, at most once a second and only when a loss moved, carries the graph's counters whole and the whole counters of each node whose counters changed since the last, and the client replaces the counters it names. A node it names that the client does not hold (ghost, removed and still closing) is ignored. A change of a card's channel count replaces the node, node.removed and node.added, and the node.added carries the counters the newer node carries on from the older (a port-caused replace is the same node to the operator: docs/engine.md#counters), so the next counters.changed moves on from them.",
